          "id": "138175c95815e33252b6fc8405164663afbab2c4",
          "message": "fix(velvet): stop cancelling a mutation when its component unmounts (#1357)\n\n## What & why\n\n`UseMutation` cancelled every call in flight when its component unmounted. TanStack Query v5 never cancels a mutation. On unmount the observer only unsubscribes, and the mutation runs to the end. So an unmount in Velvet turned a request that would have succeeded into a reported failure. A caller could not keep the request going, because the token was cancelled before their code could see the outcome.\n\n**After this change**\n- An unmount cancels nothing. A call in flight runs to the end.\n- The `UseMutation` options' `OnMutate` / `OnSuccess` / `OnError` / `OnSettled` receive the call's real outcome.\n- `MutateAsync` resolves or rejects with the function's own outcome.\n- The handle is not written after the unmount.\n- The per-call callbacks passed to `Mutate(vars, options)` are dropped after the unmount, as TanStack's observer drops them once it has no listener.\n- A call made after the unmount runs and writes no handle. Before, `MutateAsync` rejected with `OperationCanceledException`.\n- A remount of the same fiber builds fresh slots. A call still in flight from the earlier mount writes nothing into it and delivers no per-call callback there. The slot it holds is retired at the unmount.\n- `MutateOptions.CancellationToken` (new, init-only) is the caller's opt-in to cancel, which #1319 asks for. The function receives that token, or `default` if none is set. Only the caller cancels it. A cancelled call fails like any other call.\n\nThis is **breaking**. v2.1.4 cancelled the token on unmount. It is recorded in `Changelog~/breaking/claude-issue-1319-mutation-unmount.md`.\n\nThe unreleased fragment from the mutation-lifecycle change no longer describes the unmount cancellation. `Documentation~/react-migration.md` (Unmounting, Reset, the token) is updated.\n\nCloses #1319\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable). Run locally:\n  - generator suite (499 + 16)\n  - duplication, assume-gate and stranded-name checks\n  - `--refusals`\n  - `mutation_check --list` (8 mutants)\n  - `base_red_check --plan`\n\n  The Unity suites run in CI.\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it. Each new case is red on main by reading the base: the unmount cancels the token, and `MutateAsync` after an unmount throws. The remount case is red because the base lets the earlier mount's call deliver into the new mount. The two `CancellationToken` cases use the new property, so they cannot compile on main.\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (`Documentation~/react-migration.md`, `PublicAPI.txt`).\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added (`Changelog~/breaking/claude-issue-1319-mutation-unmount.md`).\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria. None.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
