          "id": "6605b828741770df151e4e70163b77548eedafab",
          "message": "feat(velvet): resolve Tailwind v4 spacing multipliers and any whole-number z-index (#1359)\n\n## What & why\n\nTailwind v4 derives every spacing utility from one `--spacing` multiplier, so any non-negative multiple of 0.25 is a valid step. Velvet only resolved the `--space-*` steps its stylesheets declare, so `p-13`, `gap-4.5`, `w-0.25` and `-top-4` resolved to nothing.\n\n**Spacing steps**\n- Every spacing utility now accepts a bare number written in canonical decimal form and resolves it to that many 4px steps. This covers:\n  - padding and margin;\n  - `gap-*` and `space-x/y-*`;\n  - `w`/`h`/`size`, `min-*` and `max-*`;\n  - `basis-*`;\n  - the insets and logical insets;\n  - `translate-x/y-*`.\n- Margin, inset, translate and space also accept a minus sign.\n- `StyleSpacingMultiplier` holds the step arithmetic, and the resolver reads it through `SpacingPrefixOf`.\n- A step the bundled stylesheets already declare stays a class.\n- The box utilities resolve every other step as inline style, the same way a bracket value resolves, and inline steps take part in the existing shorthand/longhand order.\n- `gap-*` and `space-*` steps go through the gap manipulator, as before.\n\n**Other utilities on the same scale**\n- `leading-<n>` reads the same steps. A named leading is checked first.\n- `z-<n>` accepts any whole number in the int range, negated as well, instead of only 0–50. Tailwind v4 has no cap on `z-<n>`; Velvet declines a value outside the int range, and both edges are pinned by tests.\n\n**Docs and changelog**\n- The guides changed are `styling-arbitrary-lengths.md`, `styling-flexbox-and-gap.md`, `styling-z-index.md`, `fonts.md`, `motion.md`, `react-migration.md` and the README index row.\n- A breaking fragment records that a user stylesheet class named like a newly resolved step (`.w-100`, `.p-30`) is now shadowed by the inline value.\n\nRefs #1316\n\n### Remaining\n\n#1316 also covers the blur, radius, ring, shadow and palette scales. This PR covers only the spacing multiplier and `z-<n>`; the other scales follow in separate PRs.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable)\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
