          "id": "31351bffa5387f3e33ea4906121041f1856c52ea",
          "message": "fix(velvet): hold a hidden Suspense tree's insertion effects until the reveal (#1360)\n\n## What & why\n\nWhen a `V.Suspense` boundary shows its fallback, its hidden children can still be rendered. If they were, the insertion effects that render queued could be lost before the boundary revealed them. Two cases dropped them:\n- a second render of the hidden children before the reveal;\n- a tree that had never been shown and was rendered again with unchanged deps.\n\nA component whose insertion-effect deps changed while hidden therefore never ran that effect.\n\n**React's behaviour.** On a concurrent root, React does not render or commit the primary tree while the fallback shows. `updateSuspenseComponent` bails out on the primary tree completely, leaving it in its old state with no effects. The work, and every effect it queues, runs on the reveal render. The issue originally expected insertion effects to run while the tree was hidden. That premise is corrected in the issue thread: nothing should run while hidden, and every effect owed should run once at the reveal.\n\n**The change:**\n- `FiberEffects.HoldInsertionEffects` moves a hidden fiber's pending insertion effects into `ComponentFiber.HeldInsertionEffects`. It does this before `FiberRenderer.RenderAndReconcile` clears the pending list, so a later hidden render cannot drop them.\n- `ShowLayoutEffects` merges the held effects back when the boundary reveals the fiber, without duplicates. Each one then runs once in the reveal commit.\n- The step that runs insertion effects ahead of a ref attach now skips fibers whose layout effects are hidden. Before, an attach could run a hidden fiber's insertion effects early.\n\n**Deviation.** Velvet renders the hidden children while the fallback shows, and React does not. So if an effect's deps change and then change back while hidden, the effect still runs at the reveal. `react-migration.md` records this as a Velvet deviation. The wider gap, rendering the hidden primary at all, is tracked in #1358.\n\n**Tests.** The tests are in `SuspenseHiddenInsertionEffectTests`, plus one case in `SuspendWithoutBoundaryTests`.\n- Six of the eight new cases are red on main. In each, the render on the pass that reveals the primary cleared the pending insertion effect before it could run: a first mount beside a suspending reader, a child mounted while hidden, a host re-render with changed or unchanged deps, a second render while hidden, and a hide after a first reveal.\n- The other two pin parts that already match React, the passive and layout effects of a hidden fiber waiting for the reveal, and are declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`.\n\nCloses #1313\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
